<body>
    <h1>Image Classification</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>In this article, we're gonna build a small app in <strong>SwiftU=
I</strong> that allows users to pick an image from their gallery and classi=
fy it using the pre-trained <strong>MobileNetV2</strong> model. Let=E2=80=
=99s combine CoreML and <strong>Vision Framework.</strong></p>
<p>Here=E2=80=99s how the flow works:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>A trained model (like MobileNetV2) is loaded. You can download MobileNet=
V2 on this <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://developer.apple.com/m=
achine-learning/models/" rel=3D"nofollow">link</a>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The image is processed and converted into a format the model understands=
 (<code>CIImage</code>).</p></li>
<li>
<p>The model runs using a <code>VNCoreMLRequest</code>, which returns a lis=
t of possible classifications.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The app shows the most likely prediction to the user.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>Let=E2=80=99s dive into the code!</p>
<p>First, we start by importing the necessary libraries and setting up the =
interface variables:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">import S=
wiftUI
import CoreML
import Vision
import PhotosUI

@State private var image: UIImage?
@State private var classificationLabel: String =3D "Select an image to clas=
sify"
@State private var showImagePicker: Bool =3D false
@State private var selectedItem: PhotosPickerItem? =3D nil</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Now let=E2=80=99s create the interface for our app. We need:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>An area to preview the image sent to classification.</p></li>
<li>
<p>A text label to show what the model (MobileNetV2) concluded.</p></li>
<li>
<p>A button to upload the image.</p></li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">var body=
: some View {
        VStack {
            if let image =3D image {
                Image(uiImage: image)
                    .resizable()
                    .scaledToFit()
                    .frame(height: 300)
            } else {
                Rectangle()
                    .fill(Color.secondary)
                    .frame(height: 300)
                    .overlay(
                        Text("No image selected")
                            .foregroundColor(.white)
                    )
            }

            Text(classificationLabel)
                .padding()

            ...
            ...
            ...</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>In this first part, a rectangle with the text =E2=80=9CNo image selected=
=E2=80=9D is created in case the user hasn=E2=80=99t picked anything yet. I=
f the user does choose an image, the rectangle will be replaced with it.</p=
>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">var body=
: some View {
        VStack {
            ...
            ...

            Text(classificationLabel)
                .padding()

            PhotosPicker(selection: $selectedItem, matching: .images, photo=
Library: .shared()) {
                Text("Choose Picture")
            }
            .onChange(of: selectedItem) {
                Task {
                    if let data =3D try? await selectedItem?.loadTransferab=
le(type: Data.self),
                       let uiImage =3D UIImage(data: data) {
                        image =3D uiImage
                        classifyImage(uiImage)
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        .padding()
    }</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>This second part adds the text label, which is the <code>classificationL=
abel</code> variable. If the user hasn=E2=80=99t picked any image, it=E2=80=
=99ll show =E2=80=9CSelect an image to classify.=E2=80=9D If the user has s=
elected an image, <code>classificationLabel</code> will change into whateve=
r result MobileNetV2 returns. A <code>PhotosPicker</code>button is also cre=
ated to let the user choose an image from the iPhone gallery. Once the phot=
o is picked, the code turns it into a <code>UIImage</code>, updates the scr=
een with that image, and calls the <code>classifyImage</code> function, whi=
ch takes the image and runs the classification.</p>
<p>Once the UI is done, it should look like this:</p><span class=3D"conflue=
nce-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-s=
ize"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image image-center" alt=3D"Simulator=
 Screenshot - iPhone 16 Pro - 2025-04-22 at 18.57.24.png" width=3D"299" loa=
ding=3D"lazy" src=3D"d0d496d280dc571c34e859b75c62583a4ae683a2da375ef93f9f47=
37fe239777" data-image-src=3D"https://developeracademy.atlassian.net/wiki/d=
ownload/attachments/1208877228/Simulator%20Screenshot%20-%20iPhone%2016%20P=
ro%20-%202025-04-22%20at%2018.57.24.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D=
1750692277082&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"2622" data-=
width=3D"1206" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=
=3D"1208877244" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-typ=
e=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"Simulator Screenshot=
 - iPhone 16 Pro - 2025-04-22 at 18.57.24.png" data-base-url=3D"https://dev=
eloperacademy.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"imag=
e/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"1208877228" data-linked-resourc=
e-container-version=3D"1" data-media-id=3D"c091e2e3-efe5-4485-b127-b380e9ce=
66b2" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"650"></span>
<p>Finally, let=E2=80=99s make the <code>classifyImage</code> function. Thi=
s function will be responsible for <strong>classifying the image</strong> u=
sing the <strong>MobileNetV2</strong> model. It grabs the image the user pi=
cked, processes it, runs the model, and <strong>returns a label</strong> wi=
th its classification (like <em>=E2=80=9Ccat=E2=80=9D, =E2=80=9Cdog=E2=80=
=9D, =E2=80=9Ccar=E2=80=9D</em>, etc.).</p>
<p>The first part of the code receives the image in <strong>UIImage</strong=
> format and turns it into a <strong>CIImage</strong>, since that=E2=80=99s=
 the format the Vision Framework works with.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">func cla=
ssifyImage(_ uiImage: UIImage) {
    guard let ciImage =3D CIImage(image: uiImage) else {
        classificationLabel =3D "Couldn't create CIImage from UIImage."
        return
    }
   =20
    ...
    ...</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Now let=E2=80=99s set up the pieces that load the MobileNetV2 machine le=
arning model.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">func cla=
ssifyImage(_ uiImage: UIImage) {
=09=09...
=09=09...
=09=09do {
=09=09=09=09let config =3D MLModelConfiguration()
=09=09=09=09let model =3D try MobileNetV2(configuration: config)
=09=09=09=09let visionModel =3D try VNCoreMLModel(for: model.model)</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><code>MLModelConfiguration()</code> defines the model=E2=80=99s settings=
, like whether it should run on the CPU or GPU. <code>MobileNetV2()</code>l=
oads the actual image classification model. <code>VNCoreMLModel</code> adap=
ts the model so it works with the Vision Framework.</p>
<p>Now we create the request that will classify the image:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">func cla=
ssifyImage(_ uiImage: UIImage) {
=09=09...
=09=09...
=09=09let request =3D VNCoreMLRequest(model: visionModel) { request, error =
in
=09=09    DispatchQueue.main.async {
=09=09        if let results =3D request.results as? [VNClassificationObser=
vation],
=09=09           let topResult =3D results.first {
=09=09            classificationLabel =3D "\\(topResult.identifier) (\\(Int=
(topResult.confidence * 100))%)"
=09=09        } else {
=09=09            classificationLabel =3D "No classification found."
=09=09        }
=09=09    }
=09=09}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><code>VNCoreMLRequest</code> makes the request using the model we set up=
 earlier (<strong>visionModel</strong>). Once the classification=E2=80=99s =
done, it runs the closure. The <strong>results</strong> list contains all p=
ossible classifications, and each one is a <code>VNClassificationObservatio=
n</code>type, which holds the name of the identified class and the confiden=
ce level (from 0.0 to 1.0). The code takes the most confident result and sh=
ows its name and confidence. If there are no results, it tells the user =E2=
=80=9CNo classification found.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p>Finally, let=E2=80=99s run the classification using the image the user p=
icked:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">=09=09=
=09=09let handler =3D VNImageRequestHandler(ciImage: ciImage)

=09=09=09=09DispatchQueue.global(qos: .userInitiated).async {
=09=09=09=09    do {
=09=09=09=09        try handler.perform([request])
=09=09=09=09    } catch {
=09=09=09=09        DispatchQueue.main.async {
=09=09=09=09            classificationLabel =3D "Error classifying image: \=
\(error.localizedDescription)"
=09=09=09=09        }
=09=09=09=09    }
=09=09=09=09}
=09=09} catch {
=09=09      classificationLabel =3D "Error setting up the model: \\(error.l=
ocalizedDescription)"
    }
  }
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><code>VNImageRequestHandler</code> acts like an <strong>image loader for=
 Vision</strong> =E2=80=94 it takes the image and gets it ready for the mod=
el to analyze. <code>try handler.perform([request])</code> runs the request=
 and waits for results. If anything goes wrong, the error is caught and sho=
wn to the user.</p>
<p>Here=E2=80=99s the full version of the <code>classifyImage</code> functi=
on:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: php; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">func cla=
ssifyImage(_ uiImage: UIImage) {
    guard let ciImage =3D CIImage(image: uiImage) else {
        classificationLabel =3D "Couldn't create CIImage from UIImage."
        return
    }

    do {
        let config =3D MLModelConfiguration()
        let model =3D try MobileNetV2(configuration: config)
        let visionModel =3D try VNCoreMLModel(for: model.model)
        let request =3D VNCoreMLRequest(model: visionModel) { request, erro=
r in
            DispatchQueue.main.async {
                if let results =3D request.results as? [VNClassificationObs=
ervation],
                   let topResult =3D results.first {
                    classificationLabel =3D "\\(topResult.identifier) (\\(I=
nt(topResult.confidence * 100))%)"
                } else {
                    classificationLabel =3D "No classification found."
                }
            }
        }

        let handler =3D VNImageRequestHandler(ciImage: ciImage)
        DispatchQueue.global(qos: .userInitiated).async {
            do {
                try handler.perform([request])
            } catch {
                DispatchQueue.main.async {
                    classificationLabel =3D "Error classifying image: \\(er=
ror.localizedDescription)"
                }
            }
        }
    } catch {
        classificationLabel =3D "Error setting up the model:\\(error.locali=
zedDescription)"
    }
}</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>After picking an image and running the app successfully, the screen shou=
ld look something like this:</p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wra=
pper image-center-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"co=
nfluence-embedded-image image-center" alt=3D"Simulator Screenshot - iPhone =
16 Pro - 2025-04-22 at 18.54.37.png" width=3D"299" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"=
2dd6253c66f8c71673fce1ec9cb83a92cf52047fa1a7d461580ffcf1c455c227" data-imag=
e-src=3D"https://developeracademy.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/1=
208877228/Simulator%20Screenshot%20-%20iPhone%2016%20Pro%20-%202025-04-22%2=
0at%2018.54.37.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1750692277082&amp;cac=
heVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"2622" data-width=3D"1206" data-u=
nresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"1208877247" data-l=
inked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-=
linked-resource-default-alias=3D"Simulator Screenshot - iPhone 16 Pro - 202=
5-04-22 at 18.54.37.png" data-base-url=3D"https://developeracademy.atlassia=
n.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-res=
ource-container-id=3D"1208877228" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D=
"1" data-media-id=3D"0e166d54-6900-49bc-abb3-a95d8e2ea697" data-media-type=
=3D"file" height=3D"650"></span>
<hr>
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #E6FCFF;border-width: 1px;"=
>
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #E6FCFF;">
<p>If you=E2=80=99d like to access the full source code, you can find it at=
 this <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://gist.github.com/vincenzofa=
dda/da2da7f76a13d653e593ecfe76d67e7d" rel=3D"nofollow">link</a></p>
</div>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"ImageClassification-Conclusion">Conclusion</h2>
<p>Image classification is a very popular feature in the machine learning w=
orld. In Apple=E2=80=99s ecosystem, it gets even easier to use it thanks to=
 the support from CoreML and Vision Framework. That way, developers can use=
 these models in an efficient and optimized way.</p>
<p></p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
